# Meta description (required)

Every shippable HTML page must include in `<head>`:

```html
<meta name="description" content="Descriptive, keyword-rich text that talks about the page content goes here.">
<meta name="keywords" content="comma, separated, keywords, for, this, page">
```

Rules:

- Write real page-specific **description** copy (product name + what this page does).
- Always include a visible **`meta name="keywords"`** tag with comma-separated terms (product, features, page topic).
- Prefer description ~120–160 characters; never leave placeholder text.
- Public marketing pages: indexable. Signed-in /admin pages: still include both tags (often with `noindex`).
- Shared layout/`seo()` helpers must supply both `description` and `keywords` per route.
- When adding a new view or route, add description + keywords in the same change.

Family Shield Pro: keep the “guidance, not a guarantee / never a safe stamp” voice in public descriptions.
